  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.78,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U10", "U11", "U3", "U2"],
      "pins": ["U10.7", "U11.7", "U3.7", "U2.10"],
      "nets": ["NET0019", "NET0010"],
      "observed": "On the Thermocouples sheet the SO (MISO) pin 7 of all three MAX31855KASA devices (U10, U11, U3) is driven onto the shared net NET0019, but NET0019 does not appear anywhere on the Microcontroller sheet. Conversely the ESP32-C3 (U2) pin labeled GPIO10 carries the net NET0010, and NET0010 does not appear on the Thermocouples sheet. The SCK net (NET0015) and the three CS nets (NET0011/NET0008/NET0006) are present on both sheets, so only the MISO/SO path is broken.",
      "expected": "The specification states the SPI bus is shared: 'SO (pin 7, tri-state/MISO) are common nets (SCK, SO) tied to all three ICs and to the ESP32 (U1 GPIO5/SCK, GPIO10/SO).' The thermocouple SO net must connect to the ESP32 MISO GPIO (GPIO10); the same net name must appear on both sheets.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Thermocouples sheet: U10/U11/U3 'MAX31855KASA' pin 7 SO -> NET0019 (NET0019 not present on MCU sheet)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Microcontroller sheet: ESP32-C3-MINI-1 (U2) 'GPIO10' -> NET0010 (NET0010 not present on Thermocouples sheet)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "'SO (pin 7, tri-state/MISO) are common nets (SCK, SO) tied to all three ICs and to the ESP32 (U1 GPIO5/SCK, GPIO10/SO).'"}
      ],
      "impact": "The SPI MISO line is disconnected: the ESP32 cannot read the thermocouple data word from any of the three MAX31855 chips. Temperature sensing is dead, so every zone will report a fault/zero reading and the bang-bang heater control cannot operate correctly (the firmware's ThermocoupleFault path would trip).",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing matches the spec on power arbitration, buck regulation, the high-side heater switch, fan-tach TVS protection, and the SPI SCK/CS nets, but the thermocouple SPI MISO net is broken: the shared SO net (NET0019) on the three MAX31855s never reaches the ESP32, whose GPIO10 instead carries an orphan net (NET0010). This open connection would prevent all temperature reading."
}

